[LINK: (^) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nauru#cite_ref-175]  Fabricius, Wilhelm (1992). Nauru: 1888–1900: An account in German and English based on official records of the Colonial Section of the German Foreign Office held by the Deutsches Zentralarchiv in Potsdam (PDF).  [LINK: (Canberra) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canberra] :  [LINK: (Australian National University) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Australian_National_University] . p. 271.  [LINK: (ISBN) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)]   [LINK: (978-0731513673) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-0731513673] . Archived (PDF) from the original on 27 March 2023. Retrieved 18 April 2024. The Nauruan dances which I have seen are not notable for their wealth of distinct figures. They are accompanied by singing and consist in tripping to and fro, swaying the body, slapping the thighs and chest and making turns.

